"blurb":"the Maya-pyramid-inspired icon bodega; the signature experience lets guests build their own blend guided by experts","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"private-transport DMC/affiliate 4–20%"},{"name":"Maipú bike-and-wine + olive-oil & asado","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/mendoza-travel-guide-2026-argentinas-wine-capital.htm","hook":"the casual, cyclable Maipú route linking Malbec, Bonarda, olive oil, gourmet estates, and a wood-fired asado","si":"culinary","blurb":"the casual, cyclable Maipú route linking Malbec, Bonarda, olive oil, gourmet estates, and a wood-fired asado","commission":"affiliate / DMC 4–15%"},{"name":"Achaval-Ferrer single-vineyard Malbec","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/mendoza-wine-tours-2026-best-wineries-tastings.htm","si":"culinary","commission":"DMC winery day 10–20%"},{"name":"Sunrise hot-air balloon over the vineyards","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/argentina-l168992/hot-air-balloon-ride-over-mendoza-s-vineyards-wine-toast-t876044/","hook":"~45–60 min float from the Junín/Barriales area over vine rows and olive groves with the Andes on the horizon, sparkling-wine toast on landing","si":"romance","blurb":"~45–60 min float from the Junín/Barriales area over vine rows and olive groves with the Andes on the horizon, sparkling-wine toast on landing","commission":"affiliate 4–8% / DMC bundle"},{"name":"Cacheuta thermal springs","si_tag":"romance+wellness","tier":"comfort","source":"https://thewholeworldornothing.com/hot-springs-mendoza-cacheuta-thermal-baths/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"natural Andean hot springs on the Mendoza River, multi-temperature stone pools, Argentina''s only grotto sauna, mud baths, and a Creole asado buffet","si":"romance+wellness","blurb":"natural Andean hot springs on the Mendoza River, multi-temperature stone pools, Argentina''s only grotto sauna, mud baths, and a Creole asado buffet","when":"year-round","commission":"affiliate spa day 4–8% / DMC"},{"name":"Alta Montaña + Aconcagua viewpoint + Puente del Inca","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/mendoza-l673/andes-day-trip-uspallata-aconcagua-and-puente-del-inca-t55889/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Route 7 full-day: Potrerillos Dam, Uspallata, Puente del Inca''s natural stone-and-hot-spring formation, and the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak","si":"expedition","blurb":"Route 7 full-day: Potrerillos Dam, Uspallata, Puente del Inca''s natural stone-and-hot-spring formation, and the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC / affiliate day 4–20%"},{"name":"Mendoza River rafting (Potrerillos)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://solsalute.com/blog/adventure-tourism-in-potrerillos-mendoza/","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Class II–IV depending on season/flow; certified rescue guides, kayak support, and full safety kit standard. Guided: mandatory — never run this river unguided","si":"expedition","blurb":"Class II–IV depending on season/flow; certified rescue guides, kayak support, and full safety kit standard. Guided: mandatory — never run this river unguided","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"affiliate / DMC 4–15%"},{"name":"Uspallata & the high desert","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.myguideargentina.com/experiences/mendoza-uspallata-aconcagua-and-puente-del-inca-day-trip","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"cinematic Andean valley, gateway between the wine plain and the summit corridor; horseback and 4x4 add-ons","si":"expedition","blurb":"cinematic Andean valley, gateway between the wine plain and the summit corridor; horseback and 4x4 add-ons","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC day 10–20%"}],"faq":[{"q":"Why is Mendoza the world''s Malbec capital?","a":"Because the concentration is unmatched: Argentina holds roughly 75% of the world''s Malbec vines, and about 75% of Argentina''s vineyards lie in Mendoza — making it the single most important place on the planet for the grape and the global epicenter of Malbec.","source":"winefolly.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Mendoza?","a":"Late February through April — harvest and the Fiesta Nacional de la Vendimia (2026 central acts Mar 6–10) — is the most atmospheric window. Spring (Oct–Nov) is the value-and-balance alternative, with rates running ~15–25% below harvest peaks; either way, book icon wineries and lodges 3–4 months ahead of the Feb–April peak.","source":"across-southamerica.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Which honeymoon wine-lodge should we book?","a":"The two ultra beds are Awasi Mendoza (Relais & Châteaux, Luján de Cuyo, 18 adobe rooms/villas on a ~60-acre private vineyard) and The Vines Resort & Spa (Valle de Uco, 21 private villas across 1,500 acres with vine-side dining). Both commission best through luxury consortia (Virtuoso/Fora), typically ~10%+ plus amenities.","source":"scottdunn.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you see Aconcagua on a day trip from Mendoza?","a":"Yes. Route 7 climbs the Alta Montaña corridor past Potrerillos (1,350 m), Uspallata (1,900 m), and Puente del Inca (2,720 m) to the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak, the highest in the Western Hemisphere. The day-trip tops out ~2,700 m (mild breathlessness possible); Aconcagua summit mountaineering is a separate, expedition-grade activity requiring permits and licensed guides.","source":"getyourguide.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Mendoza?","a":"Drink-driving. Wine touring plus self-drive is the single most important avoidable risk, so the standard doctrine is always a designated driver or a guided wine tour with transport — never self-drive between tastings, and ride sober on the Maipú bike-and-wine route.","source":"machupicchu.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Mendoza River rafting dangerous?","a":"Guided, it is a managed risk. Rafting at Potrerillos runs Class II–III, up to Class IV in high summer flow, with certified rescue guides, kayak safety support, and full neoprene/helmet/PFD standard — book certified operators only, and never run the river unguided.","source":"solsalute.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mendoza & Argentina Wine Country — Malbec, Valle de Uco & the Andes | TravelWell","search_language":"es-AR","local_keywords":["bodegas Mendoza","Valle de Uco vinos","Ruta del Vino Mendoza","Vendimia","Alta Montaña Aconcagua","termas de Cacheuta","Malbec de altura"],"hreflang":["en","es-AR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Awasi Mendoza (formerly Cavas Wine Lodge)","brand":"Relais & Châteaux","area":"Luján de Cuyo","product":"18 adobe rooms/villas on ~60-acre private vineyard","earning":"Virtuoso/Fora consortia commission + amenities; MoR via consortium/DMC","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"The Vines Resort & Spa","area":"Valle de Uco","product":"21 private vineyard villas on 1,500 acres + spa + vine-side dining","earning":"consortia commission + villa MoR","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Casa de Uco","area":"Valle de Uco","product":"modern estate rooms, pool + spa, working-vineyard finca","earning":"consortia / DMC commission","tier":"premier"},{"name":"Entre Cielos","area":"Luján de Cuyo","product":"design hotel in 3.2 ha Malbec vines + Hammam spa circuit","earning":"consortia / bedbank premium","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Mendoza & the Wine Country, Argentina, Argentina"},"geo":{"lat":-32.8895,"lng":-68.8458}}'::jsonb, 77),
  ('merida-mexico', '10S', 'Mérida, Yucatán', 'Mexico', 'Mérida Yucatán travel guide', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"romance","expedition","culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Capital of Yucatán state and the peninsula''s cultural + medical hub; nicknamed ''La Ciudad Blanca'' (the White City).","Yucatán is US State Department Level 1 (Exercise Normal Precautions) — one of only two Level-1 Mexican states; the safest tier.","Heart of the restored-hacienda hotel circuit — Chablé, four Luxury Collection haciendas, Angsana Xcanatún — the region''s signature luxury supply.","Distinct Yucatecan cuisine (cochinita pibil, sopa de lima, mucbipollo) centered on the 1887 Mercado Lucas de Gálvez (~2,000 stalls).","Gateway to cenote country, Celestún/Río Lagartos flamingos, Uxmal + Ruta Puuc, and Chichén Itzá; Gulf beach at Progreso ~35 min north."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Star Médica Mérida; Christus Muguerza Faro del Mayab; Centro Médico de las Américas (CMA); Clínica de Mérida — regional trauma/medical hub","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":"MID — Mérida Manuel Crescencio Rejón International (direct US: DFW, IAH, MIA)","heat":"Hot-humid May–Sep; Apr–Jun can exceed 100°F (38°C) — extreme-heat protocol on daytime ruin/cenote outings","water":"Bottled only (do not drink tap; use bottled for tooth-brushing)","malaria":"No malaria risk in Mérida / Yucatán tourist corridor; dengue present, chikungunya rising (2025–26) — mosquito precautions","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"~2026-10-25 (Hanal Pixán opening; late-Oct heat break + end of hurricane season lifts demand off baseline)","peak":"December–April (tightest Dec–March; dry-cool, low humidity)","fire_date":"2026-10-10","shoulder":"November; late April–early May","green":"May–September (hot-humid; Apr–Jun can exceed 100°F/38°C; rains peak Jun–Sep)","booking_lead":"Hacienda weddings 6–12 months (advised 10–12); leisure 1–3 months, longer for Hanal Pixán week","off_season_specials":"Summer hacienda + mansion-boutique rate softening; cenote-and-spa ''White City in the Green Season'' packaging; indoor culture year-round","event_peaks":["Hanal Pixán / Festival de las Ánimas (Oct 25–Nov 2)","Mérida Fest (early-mid January; 2026 ran Jan 5–18)","Flamingo season Nov–Feb (Celestún / Río Lagartos)"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Paseo de Montejo mansions (Casa Museo Montes Molina)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The gilded-age face of Yucatán''s ''green gold''","bookable_category":"guided walking tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.kupi.com/en-ae/explore/mexico/merida/paseo-de-montejo","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The gilded-age face of Yucatán''s ''green gold''","when":"December–April","commission":"Viator/local guide affiliate"},{"name":"Gran Museo del Mundo Maya","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The intellectual on-ramp before your first ruin","bookable_category":"entry + guided combo","tier":"essential","source":"https://travel.usnews.com/Merida_Mexico/Things_To_Do/El_Gran_Museo_del_Mundo_Maya_de_Mrida_65503/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The intellectual on-ramp before your first ruin","when":"December–April","commission":"affiliate (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Izamal — The Yellow Town + Convento de San Antonio","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The most photogenic town in Yucatán","bookable_