all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"Late spring (Mar–May) for Oct 31–Nov 2 Dia de Muertos; intent stirs summer prior","peak":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2 (rates 2–3x, ~$150–250 USD/night centro); secondary peak Guelaguetza (2026: Jul 20 & Jul 27)","fire_date":"2026-03-10","shoulder":"Nov–Apr dry/high season (best weather)","green":"Jun–Sep wet/value (lush, lower rates) except the Jul Guelaguetza spike","booking_lead":"Dia de Muertos 4–8 months (5–6 mo / May–Jun = sweet spot); Guelaguetza 3–5 months","off_season_specials":"May (post-booking lull) and late Aug–Sep (deep green, lowest occupancy) for value + villa-rung pushes","event_peaks":["Dia de Muertos (Oct 31–Nov 2)","Guelaguetza (last two Mondays of July; 2026 Jul 20 & 27)","Noche de Rabanos (Dec 23)","Semana Santa (Mar/Apr, moving)"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Monte Alban","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/monte-alban-2026-complete-unesco-archaeological-guide.htm","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"DMC/Viator half-day tour + 210 MXN INAH pass-through"},{"name":"Mitla","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","source":"https://montealbanoaxaca.com/inah-2026-entrance-fee-increases-for-monte-alban-mitla-and-other-oaxaca-archaeological-sites-updates-and-visitor-guide/","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"valley-circuit private day tour + 210 MXN INAH pass-through"},{"name":"Tlacolula Sunday market","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://oaxacatraveltips.com/tlacolula-market-oaxaca/","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"Sunday-market + villages day tour (Viator/DMC)"},{"name":"Dia de Muertos panteones","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/day-of-the-dead-oaxaca/","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"lodging + guided-experience wave (peak booking window)"},{"name":"Guelaguetza","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","source":"https://oaxacatraveltips.com/oaxaca-guelaguetza-festival/","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"ticketed-auditorium + lodging packages via DMC"},{"name":"Noche de Rabanos (Dec 23)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_of_the_Radishes","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"pre-Christmas lodging micro-spike (affiliate)"},{"name":"Casa Crespo cooking school","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","source":"https://casacrespo.com/cooking-classes/","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"Cookly/Viator marketplace"},{"name":"Mole negro tasting circuit","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.fiestamericanatravelty.com/en/grand-fiesta-americana/hotels/grand-fiesta-americana-oaxaca","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"culinary day-tour / cooking-class attach"},{"name":"Hierve el Agua","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/hierve-el-agua-oaxaca/","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"~50 MXN site entry + separate communal road toll + ~30 MXN parking, cash only, no on-site ATM. Non-commissionable","si":"expedition","blurb":"~50 MXN site entry + separate communal road toll + ~30 MXN parking, cash only, no on-site ATM. Non-commissionable","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"guided valley day-trip + ~50 MXN entry pass-through (VERIFY OPEN)"},{"name":"Santiago Matatlan mezcal route","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.oaxaca-mio.com/mezcalesdeoaxaca/matatlan.htm","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"guided mezcal-route tour (DMC/Viator); bottles non-commissionable"},{"name":"El Tule (world''s widest tree)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://culturestraveled.com/hierve-el-agua-oaxaca/","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"At Santa María del Tule, ~20 minutes from the city","si":"expedition","blurb":"At Santa María del Tule, ~20 minutes from the city","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"bundled into valley-circuit tour"},{"name":"Teotitlan del Valle weavers","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://brokenbootstravel.com/the-travelers-guide-to-teotitlan-del-valle/","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"private artisan-village tour (DMC); rug purchases direct-to-artisan"},{"name":"San Bartolo Coyotepec black pottery","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://theculturetrip.com/north-america/mexico/articles/a-tour-of-oaxacas-best-markets","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"south-valley artisan tour (DMC)"},{"name":"Alebrijes at San Martin Tilcajete","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.fiestamericanatravelty.com/en/grand-fiesta-americana/hotels/grand-fiesta-americana-oaxaca","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"artisan-workshop tour + hotel alebrije programming"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Terrain and high-proof spirits, not crime. The city is a mild **~1,555 m** (light first-day breathlessness at most); the genuine hazards are Hierve el Agua''s cliff-edge footing above a canyon and the mezcal route — high-proof tastings plus rural highway driving mean you take a driver or DMC, never self-drive after tasting.","source":"oaxacalife.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is Día de Muertos, and how far ahead do I book?","a":"Oct 31–Nov 2, and it''s the longest lead time in the inland catalog: book **4–8 months ahead** (5–6 months / May–June is the sweet spot). Walkable-Centro rooms are ~95% booked by early September and rates run **2–3× normal** ($150–250 USD/night).","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com / wheregoesrose.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Oaxaca really a top food destination?","a":"Yes — it''s widely regarded as one of the world''s great food capitals. The \"seven moles,\" market-to-table cooking schools (Casa Crespo), and the mezcal terroir of Santiago Matatlán (~45 minutes southeast, the World Capital of Mezcal) are destination-defining reasons to go.","source":"oaxaca-mio.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Is Hierve el Agua worth it — and will it be open?","a":"Worth it, but verify first. The petrified mineral \"waterfalls\" and clifftop spring-fed pools sit 70 km east near Mitla, but the site sees **periodic community-dispute closures clustering June–October** — always confirm it''s open the week before, and keep a Mitla + Tlacolula fallback ready.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Oaxaca good for couples?","a":"Yes — a slow, sensory, non-beach romance. Boutique casonas and the ex-convent (1576) Quinta Real, mezcal-tasting date nights, and the artisan-village shopping ritual (Teotitlán weaving, rugs $75–$500; San Bartolo black pottery; alebrijes) make the case.","source":"caminoreal.com / brokenbootstravel.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"romance"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Oaxaca City & the Central Valleys, Mexico — UNESCO, Mezcal, Dia de Muertos & Monte Alban | TravelWell.World","search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Dia de Muertos Oaxaca","que hacer en Oaxaca","ruta del mezcal","Guelaguetza fechas","Monte Alban precio entrada","Hierve el Agua abierto","hoteles boutique Oaxaca centro","Noche de Rabanos"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-05"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["romance","expedition"],"ultra":[{"name":"Quinta Real Oaxaca","positioning":"ex-Convent of Santa Catalina (1576), 91 rooms, UNESCO Centre","earning_path":"consortia/Virtuoso + Fora lane","mor":"hotel","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Escondido Oaxaca","positioning":"Grupo Habita design-boutique, rooftop pool","earning_path":"Grupo Habita direct + consortia/Fora","mor":"hotel","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Pug Seal Oaxaca","positioning":"top-cited Centro design-boutique","earning_path":"consortia/Fora","mor":"hotel","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Hotel Sin Nombre","positioning":"intimate quiet-luxury design hotel","earning_path":"Fora/direct","mor":"hotel","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Casa Antonieta","positioning":"9-room boutique casona, affordable-ultra entry","earning_path":"OTA + boutique-collection/Fora","mor":"hotel","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-05","hero":{"query":"Oaxaca City & the Central Valleys, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":17.0732,"lng":-96.7266}}'::jsonb, 82),
  ('ometepe-island-nicaragua', '10S', 'Ometepe Island, Nicaragua', 'Nicaragua', 'Ometepe Island', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Nicaragua', '{"wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential"}', 'essential', null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"118","emergency_fire":"128","book_enabled":false,"bin":"NO SAFE ZONE (content-only)","content_only":true,"redirect_eligible":true,"consent_flow":false,"founder_review_flag":"Political wrongful-detention risk may not register with typical leisure travelers; requires deliberate founder + compliance-attorney review before any Book path — do not soft-open on demand alone","remote_flag":true,"trauma_note":"No trauma care on-island; comprehensive care only in Managua; serious cases → Managua → US medical evacuation; long transfer times from lake island"},"timing":{"peak":"Dry season Dec–Apr (clear skies, passable hiking trails; March standout)","inflection":"Peak volume December; late-Nov/early-Dec good weather pre-rush; Nov–Feb choppy lake winds","off_season":"May–Nov green/wet — muddy trails, clouded summits","fire_date":"held — pending advisory clearance + founder/attorney"},"jewels":[{"name":"Volcán Concepción summit (1,610 m)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://ometepenicaragua.com/volcanoes/","timing":"Dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Nicaragua''s second-highest volcano and one of the most perfectly formed cones in the Americas; a serious dawn climb. price","si":"expedition","blurb":"Nicaragua''s second-highest volcano and one of the most perfectly formed cones in the Americas; a serious dawn climb. price","when":"Dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"dormant"},{"name":"Volcán Maderas summit + crater lagoon (1,394 m)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://ometepenicaragua.com/volcanoes/","timing":"Dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"dormant cone crowned by cloud forest and a still crater lake you can swim in. price","si":"expedition","blurb":"dormant cone crowned by cloud forest and a still crater lake you can swim in. price","when":"Dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"dormant"},{"name":"Río Istián kayak","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://ometepenicaragua.com/istian/index.php","hook":"moderate · guided/rental. ~4-hr paddle from Mérida through wetland channels; wildlife-rich; watch lake wind on the open-water leg","si":"expedition","blurb":"moderate · guided/rental. ~4-hr paddle from Mérida through wetland channels; wildlife-rich; watch lake wind on the open-water leg","commission":"dormant"},{"name":"San Ramón waterfall (64 m)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.theselvistaexperience.com/hiking-san-ramon-waterfall","hook":"moderate hike. ~64 m fall on Maderas above Mérida, with a swimming pool beneath","si":"expedition","blurb":"moderate hike. ~64 m fall on Maderas above Mérida, with a swimming pool beneath","commission":"dormant"},{"name":"Punta Jesús María sandbar","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://ometepenicaragua.com/charcoverde/index.php","timing":"Dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"long sandbar spit reaching into the lake, framed views of both volcanoes; classic sunset point. price","si":"expedition","blurb":"long sandbar spit reaching into the lake, framed views of both volcanoes; classic sunset point. price","when":"Dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"dormant"},{"name":"Ojo de Agua natural spring","si_tag":"wellness","tier":"essential","source":"https://ometepenicaragua.com/volcanoes/","timing":"Dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"underground-fed mineral swimming holes between the volcanoes; the island''s slow-morning ritual. price","si":"wellness","blurb":"underground-fed mineral swimming holes between the volcanoes; the island''s slow-morning ritual. price","when":"Dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"dormant"},{"name":"Charco Verde Nature Reserve","si_tag":"wellness","tier":"essential","source":"https://travelmademedoit.com/charco-verde-ometepe/","timing":"Dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"algae-green lagoon and lake beaches on Concepción''s south side, with the Mirador del Diablo lookout above. price","si":"wellness","blurb":"algae-green lagoon and lake beaches on Concepción''s south side, with the Mirador del Diablo lookout above. price","when":"Dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"dormant"},{"name":"Pre-Columbian petroglyphs (1,700+)","si_tag":"Culture/Romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.dreambigtravelfarblog.com/blog/ometepe-nicaragua","timing":"Dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"1,700+ carvings across 100+ sites; densest at Finca Magdalena; half-submerged carved stones near Tichana past San Ramón. price","si":"Culture/Romance","blurb":"1,700+ carvings across 100+ sites; densest at Finca Magdalena; half-submerged carved stones near Tichana past San Ramón. price","when":"Dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"dormant"}],"faq":[{"q":"What makes Ometepe Island special?","a":"Ometepe is the largest island in a freshwater lake in the world and a UNESCO Biosphere Reserve since 2010, formed by two volcanoes — active Concepción (1,610 m) and dormant Maderas (1,394 m) — joined by the Isthmus of Istián across roughly 276 km². It also holds over 1,700 pre-Columbian petroglyphs across more than 100 documented sites.","source":"en.unesco.org; lacgeo.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"How hard are the Ometepe volcano hikes?","a":"Both are serious. Concepción is a strenuous ~10-hour dawn-start climb; Maderas is ~8 hours via a ~4.5 km trail from Balgüe / Finca Magdalena, with a crater lagoon you can swim in at the summit. A licensed local guide is mandatory for both because the upper slopes are exposed, muddy, and cloud-forest-slick.","source":"ometepenicaragua.com; alongdustyroads.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where can you swim on Ometepe?","a":"Ojo de Agua (\"eye of the water\") is the island''s signature spot — a natural mineral swimming hole fed by an underground river originating on Volcán Maderas, about 2 km from Santo Domingo. Go early or late to avoid crowds. Maderas'' summit crater lagoon and designated lake beaches are the other locally advised swims.","source":"ometepenicaragua.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"wellness"},{"q":"Where do couples stay on Ometepe?","a":"Ometepe skews to off-grid eco-lodges rather than resorts. Totoco Eco-Lodge (8 design cabins on Maderas'' slopes, lake-and-Concepción views, farm-to-table dining), Finca del Sol (a 100% sustainable eco-lodge with permaculture farm), and Hacienda Mérida give the quiet, unscripted, two-people-and-a-volcano energy.","source":"steppestravel.com; hotelfincadelsol.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Two things: political detention and remoteness. Per the State Department, US nationals face serious risk of wrongful detention, exit bans, and detentions of weeks-plus, with some crimes carrying 50+ year sentences. And there is no trauma-grade care on-island — comprehensive care exists only in Managua, so a serious case realistically means Managua then a US medical evacuation.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is climbing an active volcano here dangerous?","a":"Concepción is an active stratovolcano (its last significant ash event was March 2010), and its summit hike is strenuous, exposed, and dawn-started; Maderas is dormant but steep, muddy, and cloud-forest-slick. A licensed guide is mandatory on both, and you should check volcanic status before going — though all of this fires as content only under the Level 3 advisory.","source":"ometepenicaragua.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-NI","local_keywords":["Isla de Ometepe qué hacer","Volcán Concepción","Volcán Maderas laguna cráter","Ojo de Agua Ometepe","cascada San Ramón Ometepe","kayak Río Istián","petroglifos Ometepe","ferry San Jorge Ometepe"],"hreflang":["en","es-NI"],"primary_keyword":"Ometepe Island"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"wellness","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Totoco Eco-Lodge","location":"Balgüe","price_tier":"mid/boutique-eco","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://www.steppestravel.com/accommodation/totoco-eco-lodge/"},{"name":"Finca del Sol Eco Lodge","location":"Maderas base","price_tier":"mid/eco","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://hotelfincadelsol.com/"},{"name":"Hacienda Mérida","location":"Mérida","price_tier":"value/mid","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://www.hmerida.com/espanol/activity/1"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Ometepe Island, Nicaragua, Nicaragua"},"geo":{"lat":11.5,"lng":-85.5833}}'::jsonb, 83),
