oa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov–Apr (dry season, jungle passable, waterfalls turquoise)","inflection":"early–mid September","fire_date":"late August (curve-start − 1–2 weeks)","off_season":"May–Oct rainy — brown water, muddy roads, higher road risk"},"jewels":[{"name":"Temple of the Inscriptions + Pakal''s pyramid","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://mayaruins.com/palenque/a1_223.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the anchor. Tomb descent closed since ~2004; regalia at the site museum","si":"culture","blurb":"the anchor. Tomb descent closed since ~2004; regalia at the site museum","when":"year-round","commission":"guided-tour DMC/affiliate (admission non-commissionable)"},{"name":"The Palace + observation tower","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/palenque-ruins-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the four-story tower is Palenque''s signature silhouette; the Palace complex is the civic heart of the site","si":"culture","blurb":"the four-story tower is Palenque''s signature silhouette; the Palace complex is the civic heart of the site","when":"year-round","commission":"guided-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Site Museum + Pakal reconstructed tomb exhibit","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://mayaruins.com/palenque/a1_223.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"bundled admission (non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Bonampak murals (~792 AD)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Palenque/Tour-Bonampak-and-Yaxchilan/d23479-30922P9","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"best-preserved Classic Maya murals on Earth, full-color three-room cycle","si":"culture","blurb":"best-preserved Classic Maya murals on Earth, full-color three-room cycle","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"full-day DMC tour"},{"name":"Yaxchilán by Usumacinta riverboat","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Palenque/Tour-Bonampak-and-Yaxchilan/d23479-30922P9","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Usumacinta motorboat into the Lacandón, ruins the road cannot reach","si":"culture","blurb":"Usumacinta motorboat into the Lacandón, ruins the road cannot reach","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"licensed river-tour DMC (border-verify)"},{"name":"Agua Azul cascades","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Palenque/Agua-Azul-and-Misol-Ha/d23479-30922P10","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"waterfall day-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Misol-Ha waterfall (Predator site)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-palenque/","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"day-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Roberto Barrios cascades","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://nomadearthcatalog.com/cascadas-roberto-barrios/","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"five off-the-beaten-track falls, turquoise pools, natural 10 m slide, ~45 min south, entry ~30 MXN","si":"expedition","blurb":"five off-the-beaten-track falls, turquoise pools, natural 10 m slide, ~45 min south, entry ~30 MXN","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"dedicated day-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Howler-monkey jungle canopy (dawn ruins)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.timetravelturtle.com/mexico/visit-palenque/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the sound that defines dawn at Palenque; the ruins double as a wildlife encounter","si":"expedition","blurb":"the sound that defines dawn at Palenque; the ruins double as a wildlife encounter","when":"year-round","commission":"guided dawn tour upsell"},{"name":"Lacandón Jungle multi-day expedition","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://mayantourstravel.com/tours/the-amazing-lacandon-jungle-groups/","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"deep-forest circuit combining Bonampak, Yaxchilán and river camps","si":"expedition","blurb":"deep-forest circuit combining Bonampak, Yaxchilán and river camps","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"multi-day DMC"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for — is the road dangerous?","a":"The road is the risk, not the ruins. The overland San Cristóbal↔Palenque highway via Ocosingo (Chilón) has a documented armed-robbery history — one reported incident had ~18 men with assault rifles set a roadblock and rob a line of tourist vehicles, with the worst incidents after dark. The rule is daytime-only, guided/convoy transfer, no self-drive, and the safer, longer Villahermosa toll-road approach where possible.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com / jeniastraveldiaries.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How remote is medical care from Palenque?","a":"Genuinely remote — plan for it. Palenque is a small town with limited advanced care; serious trauma routes to Villahermosa or Tuxtla Gutiérrez, with air evacuation to Mexico City for anything major. Bonampak, Yaxchilán and the deep-jungle waterfalls are hours from a hospital, so carry evacuation insurance — and note dengue is present year-round with malaria risk in rural Chiapas.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What will I see at the Palenque ruins?","a":"A Maya city the rainforest never fully released: the Temple of the Inscriptions rising over Pakal the Great''s tomb, and the four-story observation tower of the Palace, its civic heart. The tomb chamber itself has been closed to descent since ~2004 to protect it, so you see the pyramid and Pakal''s regalia at the site museum, not the crypt. Go at the 8 AM opening before the jungle heat.","source":"mayaruins.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What are the Palenque waterfalls, and when should I go?","a":"Three systems within reach: Agua Azul''s 500+ turquoise cascades over ~6 km, the ~35 m Misol-Ha plunge with a walk-behind grotto, and the quieter Roberto Barrios falls with a natural rock slide (~45 min south, entry ~30 MXN). Come November–April, when the mineral-rich water runs brilliant turquoise; in the May–October rains sediment turns Agua Azul brown. Swim only in marked zones — currents are strong.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can I visit Bonampak and Yaxchilán?","a":"Yes, as a full-day guided expedition. Bonampak holds the best-preserved Classic Maya murals in existence (~792 AD), and Yaxchilán is reachable only by motorboat on the Usumacinta River, the water border with Guatemala. Go with a licensed operator, not an ad-hoc boatman, verify current border and security conditions before booking, and travel by daylight with life vests.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Palenque, Mexico: Jungle Maya Ruins, Waterfalls & Safe Travel Guide (2026) | TravelWell","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["ruinas de Palenque","Agua Azul Chiapas","Misol-Ha","Yaxchilán Bonampak","cascadas Roberto Barrios","Templo de las Inscripciones Pakal","cómo llegar a Palenque desde Villahermosa"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Palenque"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Chan-Kah Resort Village","tier":"premier","mor":"bedbank/direct","earning":"modest — upper-mid ADR, not luxury; live"},{"name":"Boutique Quinta Chanabnal","tier":"premier","mor":"advisor/direct","earning":"modest"},{"name":"Piedra de Agua Palenque","tier":"comfort","mor":"verify","earning":"to verify"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Palenque, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":17.484,"lng":-92.046}}'::jsonb, 85),
  ('pantanal-brazil', '10S', 'The Pantanal, Brazil', 'Brazil', 'The Pantanal', 'live', 'verified', 'safariJeep', 'Amazon, Pantanal & Iguaçu', '{"safari","wildlife","expedition"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"190","emergency_secondary":["193 fire/environmental","192 SAMU medical"],"advisory_level":"L2","advisory_note":"L2 (Brazil) — Pantanal exempted; route to the park","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access":{"north":"CGB (Cuiabá) — Porto Jofre / Transpantaneira","south":"CGR (Campo Grande) — Caiman / Southern reserves"},"remote_flag":true,"medevac_note":"hours by dirt road + river to trauma care (Cuiabá north / Campo Grande south); comprehensive insurance w/ medical evacuation is a standard attach","health":{"malaria":"low; zone-dependent (present in parts of state of Mato Grosso / Northern; NOT in Cuiabá city nor Mato Grosso do Sul / Southern)","dengue_chikungunya":"flag — present; insect protection regardless of malaria zone","yellow_fever":"vaccination recommended for Mato Grosso"},"wildlife_water_rules":["life vests on all boat safaris","no-approach / minimum-distance on jaguars","no swimming in caiman/piranha waters","stay in vehicle/boat","no feeding or baiting"],"fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Amazonas State FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the following river areas towards the west of Amazonas State: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State There are risks to travellers in river areas towards the west of Amazonas State, where Brazil shares borders with Colombia, Peru and Venezuela, due to criminal activity."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/brazil","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-11T12:32:48+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Dry season Jul-Oct; jaguar optimum late Jul-early Oct; strongest Aug-Sep","birding":"year-round; jabiru nesting Jul-early Nov; wading-bird flocks late Jul-mid-Aug","high_water_green_season":"Dec-Mar (rivers highest, jaguars dispersed, lush + cheaper)","inflection":"demand loads 6+ months ahead of dry season; premium Porto Jofre beds scarce","fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks; fire in Nov-Jan of prior season for the Jul-Oct jaguar peak","advance_book_note":"jaguar-season lodges (floating suites, mobile camps, top river lodges) book 6+ months out for Aug-Sep","off_season_fill":"green season Dec-Mar sold on price + birding + photography + fewer boats"},"jewels":[{"name":"Porto Jofre jaguar boat safari","si_tag":"safari","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.flashpackerconnect.com/blog/the-ultimate-guide-to-jaguar-viewing-tours-in-brazils-pantanal","timing":"Dry season Jul-Oct","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Small open boats on the Cuiabá/Piquirí/Três Irmãos rivers. Guide-required","si":"safari","blurb":"Small open boats on the Cuiabá/Piquirí/Três Irmãos rivers. Guide-required","when":"Dry season Jul-Oct",