 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"December–April (dry season; whales Dec–Mar; holiday + wedding season)","inflection":"late September–October (winter-escape lock-in)","fire_date":"2026-09-15","fire_date_note":"curve-start minus 1–2 weeks; villa/resort weddings book 9–12 months out (peak-wedding cohort ~12+ mo prior)","off_season_fill":"May–October green season (value; overlaps peak dengue May–Nov)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Private-chef villa evening","si_tag":"romance","tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.puntademita-realestate.com/vacationrentals/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Estate villa + in-villa private chef + sommelier for a proposal, anniversary, or wedding-eve dinner over Banderas Bay","si":"romance","blurb":"Estate villa + in-villa private chef + sommelier for a proposal, anniversary, or wedding-eve dinner over Banderas Bay","when":"December–April","commission":"villa MoR/specialist + Fora/Virtuoso (resort residences); DMC chef","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Susurros del Corazón wedding","si_tag":"romance","tier":"ultra","source":"https://aubergeresorts.com/susurros/events/weddings/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"\"Whispers of the Heart\" — jungled cliffs to a private beach, event spaces for 30–300, ~45 min from PVR","si":"romance","blurb":"\"Whispers of the Heart\" — jungled cliffs to a private beach, event spaces for 30–300, ~45 min from PVR","when":"December–April","commission":"Auberge → Fora/Virtuoso + wedding DMC","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Litibú beach","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.puntamita.com/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","hook":"The quieter, wilder Punta Mita beach — long sand, surf, and the Bahía golf course backdrop; a slower counterpoint to the resort core","si":"tropical","blurb":"The quieter, wilder Punta Mita beach — long sand, surf, and the Bahía golf course backdrop; a slower counterpoint to the resort core","commission":"villa/resort night + DMC transfer","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"El Anclote beach + beach clubs","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"comfort","source":"https://thesurfatlas.com/surfing-mexico/punta-mita-surf/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","hook":"The peninsula''s social beach — beginner surf, beach-club dining, the whale-tour pier","si":"tropical","blurb":"The peninsula''s social beach — beginner surf, beach-club dining, the whale-tour pier","commission":"affiliate dining/activity + resort night","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Sayulita / San Pancho day","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.rivieranayarit.com/activity/water/tour-marietas-island-hidden-beach-punta-mita/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Bohemian surf-and-art villages ~30–45 min north — day-out contrast to Punta Mita polish","si":"tropical","blurb":"Bohemian surf-and-art villages ~30–45 min north — day-out contrast to Punta Mita polish","when":"December–April","commission":"DMC day-tour + affiliate activity","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Jack Nicklaus Pacífico — Tail of the Whale","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://nicklausdesign.com/course/puntamita/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","hook":"The world''s only natural-island par-3 green, 199 yds offshore, walkable at low tide; 7,104-yd par-72 with eight ocean holes","si":"expedition","blurb":"The world''s only natural-island par-3 green, 199 yds offshore, walkable at low tide; 7,104-yd par-72 with eight ocean holes","commission":"golf package via resort/DMC + Fora/Virtuoso resort night","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Bahía course (Nicklaus 2009)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://nicklausdesign.com/course/puntamita2/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"360° Banderas Bay views, a beach hole by the El Faro surf spot; the more technical of the two","si":"expedition","blurb":"360° Banderas Bay views, a beach hole by the El Faro surf spot; the more technical of the two","when":"December–April","commission":"golf package + resort","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Islas Marietas — Playa del Amor","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islas_Marietas_National_Park (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"SEMARNAT-permitted crater beach reached by swimming a cave tunnel; ~116 visitors/day, Wed–Sun, ~15-min boat","si":"expedition","blurb":"SEMARNAT-permitted crater beach reached by swimming a cave tunnel; ~116 visitors/day, Wed–Sun, ~15-min boat","when":"December–April","commission":"SEMARNAT-permitted operator (non-commissionable park fee) + resort night","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Humpback whale-watching, Banderas Bay","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://villaexperience.com/whale-watching-punta-mita-guide-2026/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","hook":"300–500 humpbacks each Dec–Mar; El Anclote pier to sighting zones in 15–30 min","si":"expedition","blurb":"300–500 humpbacks each Dec–Mar; El Anclote pier to sighting zones in 15–30 min","commission":"licensed operator + Fora/Virtuoso resort","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"El Anclote / La Lancha surf","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://wildmex.com/activities/surfing-punta-mita-surf-lessons/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","hook":"Beginner cove + the region''s best peeling waves; guided lessons $60–180 depending on group/private","si":"expedition","blurb":"Beginner cove + the region''s best peeling waves; guided lessons $60–180 depending on group/private","commission":"surf school (affiliate/DMC) + resort","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Rip currents and dengue, not crime. The Pacific beaches have rip currents and shore break — swim guarded resort beaches and obey the flags — and Nayarit is a high-prevalence dengue state with a May–November transmission peak, so pack repellent for summer stays. Nearest full trauma is Puerto Vallarta (~40 min), then US air-evac.","source":"travel.state.gov / cdc.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Punta Mita good for a destination wedding?","a":"It is one of Mexico''s ultra-wedding flagships. Susurros del Corazón (Auberge) alone hosts events for 30–300 guests ~45 minutes from PVR, with reception rental from $2,000, alongside Four Seasons and St. Regis event teams. Villa and resort weddings book 9–12 months out — peak-season cohorts 12+ months.","source":"aubergeresorts.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the best beach and surf for beginners?","a":"El Anclote. It''s a sheltered, sandy-bottom cove with gentle rolling waves — the peninsula''s beginner classroom — while La Lancha, a ~10-minute jungle-trail walk away, holds the most reliable quality waves for confident beginners through intermediates. Guided lessons ($60–180) stage away from the rocks.","source":"thesurfatlas.com / wildmex.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is the golf as good as they say?","a":"Yes — it''s a two-course Nicklaus complex with a genuine one-of-a-kind hole. The Pacífico course (7,104-yd par-72, eight ocean holes) has the \"Tail of the Whale,\" the world''s only natural-island green, 199 yards offshore and walkable at low tide; the 2009 Bahía course is the more technical of the two.","source":"nicklausdesign.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"How do I actually visit the Islas Marietas Hidden Beach?","a":"Only with a SEMARNAT-permitted operator, and book weeks ahead. Playa del Amor is capped at ~116 visitors/day, Wed–Sun, reached by a ~15-minute boat then a life-jacketed swim through a low cave tunnel; non-swimmers can''t access it. Never promise a landing without a confirmed permitted slot.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"ocean-adventures-—-future"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Punta Mita, Mexico — Ultra-Luxury Resorts, Private Villas & Whale Season | TravelWell","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["Punta Mita resorts","villas Punta Mita","Four Seasons Punta Mita","bodas Punta Mita","avistamiento de ballenas Riviera Nayarit","Islas Marietas Playa del Amor","golf Punta Mita"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"property":"Four Seasons Resort Punta Mita","rooms":"~173 incl. 30 suites + private villas","path":"Fora/Virtuoso","value_add":"FS Preferred credit / upgrade / breakfast","tier":"ultra"},{"property":"The St. Regis Punta Mita","rooms":"89 rooms + 31 suites, butler service","path":"Fora/Virtuoso","value_add":"Marriott Luminous/STARS","tier":"ultra"},{"property":"Susurros del Corazón (Auberge)","rooms":"89 keys (59 rooms/suites + 30 villas)","path":"Fora/Virtuoso + wedding DMC","value_add":"Auberge preferred","tier":"ultra"},{"property":"Conrad Punta de Mita","rooms":"Hilton ultra-resort","path":"Fora/Virtuoso","value_add":"Hilton Impresario","tier":"ultra"},{"property":"Branded private villas (FS / St. Regis / Auberge residences)","rooms":"3–6BR oceanfront estates w/ pools","path":"Fora/Virtuoso or specialist MoR","value_add":"villa-week commission + resort value-add","tier":"ultra"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Punta Mita, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.77,"lng":-105.52}}'::jsonb, 92),
