26-07-07"},{"name":"Coffee-finca tour + cupping (Apaneca / Ataco)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.visitelsalvador.ai/blog/ruta-de-las-flores-guide-complet-villages | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"DMC add-on or Santa Leticia direct-stay bundle; operator/hotel commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Santa Ana volcano turquoise crater + Cerro Verde","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://sallysees.com/santa-ana-volcano-hike/ | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The signature GEA hero shot — a radioactive-bright sulphur lake in an active crater","si":"expedition","blurb":"The signature GEA hero shot — a radioactive-bright sulphur lake in an active crater","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"Guided-summit product via DMC/Viator; guiding/transport commissionable, park fees not","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Lake Coatepeque (volcanic caldera lake)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.booking.com/city/sv/coatepeque.html | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"Lakeside boutique-hotel bookings (Cardedeu/Equinoccio) + boat excursions via operator","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Apaneca Laguna Verde + Enganches/Ausol canopy zipline","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.visitelsalvador.ai/blog/ruta-de-las-flores-guide-complet-villages | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Crater lake ~5 km from Apaneca plus Central America''s longest cloud-forest ziplines","si":"expedition","blurb":"Crater lake ~5 km from Apaneca plus Central America''s longest cloud-forest ziplines","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"DMC/operator activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Los Chorros de la Calera / Siete Cascadas waterfall hike (Juayúa)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.visitelsalvador.ai/blog/ruta-de-las-flores-guide-complet-villages | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Terraced falls with cliff jumps and rappels. The 7 Waterfalls hike requires a mandatory guide — flash-flood, slick-rock, and cliff-jump hazards make guided mandatory","si":"expedition","blurb":"Terraced falls with cliff jumps and rappels. The 7 Waterfalls hike requires a mandatory guide — flash-flood, slick-rock, and cliff-jump hazards make guided mandatory","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"Local guide via DMC; commissionable through operator (guided-only)","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Concepción de Ataco street art + coffee","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.visitelsalvador.ai/blog/ruta-de-las-flores-guide-complet-villages | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"El Salvador''s most photogenic mural town — indigenous-history murals, Mirador de la Cruz, indigo-dye workshops, weekend street festival","si":"culture","blurb":"El Salvador''s most photogenic mural town — indigenous-history murals, Mirador de la Cruz, indigo-dye workshops, weekend street festival","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"Mural-walk + coffee-finca combo via DMC; workshop fees via operator","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Nahuizalco Mercado Nocturno (night market)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.visitelsalvador.ai/blog/ruta-de-las-flores-guide-complet-villages | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"One of the few places you''ll see women in traditional Pipil dress; wicker-craft workshops and a rare evening artisan market","si":"culture","blurb":"One of the few places you''ll see women in traditional Pipil dress; wicker-craft workshops and a rare evening artisan market","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"Evening add-on to route itinerary; craft purchases direct","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Joya de Cerén — Pompeii of the Americas (UNESCO)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/San-Salvador-attractions/Joya-de-Ceren-Archaeological-Site/d5585-a15755 | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"A 7th-century Maya farming village buried and preserved by volcanic ash; El Salvador''s only UNESCO World Heritage site. Open 9–4, closed Mondays; on-site museum","si":"culture","blurb":"A 7th-century Maya farming village buried and preserved by volcanic ash; El Salvador''s only UNESCO World Heritage site. Open 9–4, closed Mondays; on-site museum","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"Guided heritage day trip via DMC/Viator; site entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Tazumal ruins (Chalchuapa)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://andysworldjourneys.com/2025/10/16/joya-de-ceren-and-tazumal-ancient-history-in-el-salvador/ | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"El Salvador''s most important pyramids/ceremonial platforms, ~40 min from Joya de Cerén — the two pair into one Maya-heritage day","si":"culture","blurb":"El Salvador''s most important pyramids/ceremonial platforms, ~40 min from Joya de Cerén — the two pair into one Maya-heritage day","when":"year-round","commission":"Combined Maya-heritage day trip w/ Joya de Cerén via DMC/operator; entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the Juayúa food festival?","a":"The Feria Gastronómica is the route''s flagship weekend market: every Saturday and Sunday, 11am–5pm, free entry, cash only, with the plaza filling with grills and pots — grilled meats $6–9, seafood ~$7, soups $3–4, pupusas ~$0.60, and roughly $10–20 feeds one person across multiple dishes. *[Culinary]*","source":"visitelsalvador.ai, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Is Joya de Cerén worth visiting?","a":"Yes — it is El Salvador''s only UNESCO World Heritage site, a 7th-century Maya farming village buried and preserved by volcanic ash, earning the name \"Pompeii of the Americas.\" Open 9–4 and closed Mondays with an on-site museum, it pairs with the Tazumal ruins (~$5 entry, ~40 min away) into one Maya-heritage day. *[Culture & Heritage]*","source":"viator.com + andysworldjourneys.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is the Santa Ana volcano hike dangerous?","a":"It is managed, not casual. Santa Ana (Volcán Ilamatepec, 2,381 m) is an active, monitored volcano with a turquoise sulphur crater lake and volcanic gas near the rim; the ~4–5 hour summit hike is guided-only, at scheduled departure times, and is subject to closure on activity alerts. Do not attempt it unguided, and confirm open status before booking.","source":"sallysees.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What outdoor adventures are on the Ruta de las Flores?","a":"The GEA spine runs from Santa Ana''s turquoise crater and Cerro Verde to Lake Coatepeque (a volcanic caldera lake beneath the volcano), plus Apaneca''s cloud-forest canopy ziplines (Los Enganches ~420 m lines) and the Laguna Verde crater lake ~5 km from Apaneca. Waterfall hikes at Los Chorros / Siete Cascadas round it out. *[GEA]*","source":"visitelsalvador.ai + sallysees.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where do couples stay on the Ruta de las Flores?","a":"Two romance bookends: coffee-finca boutique on the route itself — Hotel Santa Leticia, a 19-room working-estate lodge from ~USD 78/night — or lakeside luxe on Lake Coatepeque, where Cardedeu Residence is a 5-star hotel and Equinoccio a boutique lakeside stay with balcony rooms over the water. There is no international five-star flag on the route. *[Romance]*","source":"lastfrontiers.com + booking.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Guided-only adventure and mountain roads. The Siete Cascadas 7-waterfall hike (~6 hrs) requires a mandatory guide (~$15/person) because of flash-flood, slick-rock, and cliff-jump hazards; canopy ziplines are operator-run with harness and briefing. The route itself is a cobblestone-and-switchback mountain drive — go in daylight, watch for highland fog, and prefer a local driver at night.","source":"visitelsalvador.ai, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Ruta de las Flores, El Salvador — Coffee Towns, Santa Ana Volcano & the Flower Route | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","search_language":"es-SV","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","local_keywords":["Ruta de las Flores El Salvador","Volcán Santa Ana","Juayúa festival gastronómico","Concepción de Ataco murales","Laguna Verde Apaneca","tour de café Ruta de las Flores","Lago de Coatepeque hotel","Joya de Cerén Pompeya de América"],"hreflang":["en","es-SV"],"primary_keyword":"Ruta de las Flores"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"},{"si":"culinary","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"property":"Hotel & Restaurante Santa Leticia (Apaneca)","note":"Boutique coffee-finca ceiling on the route itself; 19 rooms, on-farm coffee program","earning":"hotel commission via consortia/bedbank","mor":"hotel/OTA","tier":"$$–$$$"},{"property":"Cardedeu (5-star) / Equinoccio + private villas, Lake Coatepeque","note":"Caldera-lake luxe bookend under Santa Ana","earning":"hotel commission (Cardedeu/Equinoccio); villas referral/affiliate only","mor":"hotel for flags; Airbnb/VRBO for villas","tier":"$$$–$$$$"},{"property":"San Salvador city 5-star bookend","note":"Arrival/departure luxe anchor; where international-flag commission lives (verify availability)","earning":"hotel commission via preferred/Virtuoso program","mor":"hotel","tier":"$$$–$$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Ruta de las Flores, El Salvador, El Salvador"},"geo":{"lat":13.8722,"lng":-89.7928}}'::jsonb, 96),
  ('san-blas-guna-yala-panama', '10S', 'San Blas / Guna Yala, Panama', 'Panama', 'Guna Yala, island by island', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Panama', '{"tropical","romance","expedition","culture"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_date":"2024-09-23 (reissued; verified live 2026-07-07)","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":"Charter flights Albrook (PAC) → El Porvenir (PVE) / Corazón de Jesús (CZJ), ~40–45 min, ~$400/pax; OR 4x4 (steep rain-sensitive Cartí road, ~4–5 hrs) + boat, through Guna Cartí checkpoint (passport + ~$20/pax foreigner entry fee, cash, no ATMs)","remote_flag":true,"medevac_note":"No hospital in Guna Yala; most cays have no clinic; serious cases require medevac to Panama City / US (can exceed $50,000) — comprehensive medevac insurance mandatory","health_note":"Year-round dengue/malaria/zika/chikungunya risk; malaria-risk area — consult travel clinic on prophylaxis; drink bottled/treated water","gate_result":"PASS — Guna Yala/San Blas verified NOT in any L4/L3 named area of the Sept 23, 2024 Panama advisory (Level 2 country-wide). Bin = freely bookable (L2). Verified live 2026-07-07.","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/panama","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2025-12-10T13:26:25+00:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"dry season Dec–Apr (calmer seas for sailing + the Colombia crossing)","inflection":"Oct–Nov (winter-escape + honeymoon + dry-season sailing dates on sale)","fire_date":"mid-to-late September (curve-start − 1–2 weeks); charters sell out ahead","off_season":"May–Nov green/rainy — value + solitude window, weather-tolerant travelers"},"jewels":[{"name":"Cayos Holandeses (Dutch Cays) sandbar","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.seasanblas.com/blog/cayos-holandeses-one-of-the-best-san-blas-islands-to-visit","timing":"dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the remote outer cluster — is widely rated the best snorkeling in the San Blas archipelago","si":"Tropical/Beaches","blurb":"the remote outer cluster — is widely rated the best snorkeling in the San Blas archipelago","when":"dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"multi-day charter / premium day-trip via DMC"},{"name":"Natural Pool / Starfish spot (Piscina Natural)","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.seasanblas.com/blog/complete-guide-to-visiting-san-blas-islands-panama","timing":"dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical/Beaches","when":"dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"island-hopping day tour via DMC"},{"name":"Isla Pelícano / Cayos Limones lagoon","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"essential","source":"https://nomadsailors.com/blog/cayos-limones/","timing":"dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical/Beaches","when":"dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"day tour / short cabaña stay"},{"name":"Castaway-island overnight cabaña","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotels-g298434-San_Blas_Islands_Guna_Yala_Region-Hotels.html","timing":"dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"DMC cabaña package or private charter overnight"},{"name":"Isla Perro (Dog Island) wreck snorkel","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://sanblasadventures.com/san-blas-snorkeling/","si":"expedition","commission":"day tour / charter stop"},{"name":"Panama → Cartagena sailing charter (3–5 days)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://sanblasadventures.com/boat-colombia-to-panama/general-information/","si":"expedition","commission":"charter / CLIA lane — highest-value bookable in region"},{"name":"Guna mola textiles + living culture (1925 revolution, matrilineal congress, Dulegaya)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage (future)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tourismpanama.com/culture-cuisine/indigenous-communities/guna/","timing":"dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Culture & Heritage (future)","when":"dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"cultural add-on / community visit via DMC (direct artisan purchases non-commissionable)"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in San Blas?","a":"Remoteness, not crime. There is no hospital and, on most cays, no clinic; serious illness or injury means evacuation to Panama City or the US, which can exceed $50,000. Comprehensive travel + medevac insurance is a condition of going, not an option — and dengue/malaria risk is year-round.","source":"smartraveller.gov.au, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Are the boat crossings and the 4x4 access road dangerous?","a":"Manageable but weather-governed. Everything moves by open boat, so insist on worn life vests, a licensed captain, and a real forecast check; the Colombia passage is 24–52 hours at open sea with no turning back mid-crossing. The overland Cartí route is a steep, rain-sensitive mountain road needing a 4x4 (4–5 hours). Guided only.","source":"sanblasadventures.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Which San Blas islands are best for beaches and snorkeling?","a":"The outer Cayos Holandeses (Dutch Cays) are widely rated the best snorkeling in the archipelago, with healthy reef and cushion starfish on the flats. Isla Perro holds the signature shallow-shipwreck snorkel a few metres from shore, while the Cayos Limones lagoon (Isla Pelícano, of *Money Heist* fame) offers the easiest crystal-shallow day-trip.","source":"seasanblas.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is San Blas good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes, if you want elemental over polished. The set-piece is a private or near-private sand-cay cabaña — hammock, palm, reef at the doorstep, no wifi — from ~$56–$100/night full-board, scaling up to a private crewed catamaran overnight. Expect solar power and often no running water: this is the Caribbean before anyone built a lobby on it.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What is the Panama-to-Cartagena sailing trip like?","a":"It''s a genuine passage, not a lagoon cruise. Three days threading the San Blas cays, then 24–52 hours of open-water crossing to Colombia; shared cabins run ~$525–$750 (meals + immigration paperwork included), private from ~$900+. Small boats have limited cabins and sell out weeks ahead for dry-season departures.","source":"sanblasadventures.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Who are the Guna, and how do I enter the comarca?","a":"You enter on Guna terms. The Guna are a matrilineal people who won semi-autonomy in the 1925 revolution and still govern by congress under saila leaders; entry means a passport check and a per-person cash fee (~$20/foreigner) at the Cartí checkpoint, with no ATMs on the islands. Buy reverse-appliqué molas direct from the women who sew them.","source":"ampatours.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Blas Islands (Guna Yala), Panama — Castaway Cays, Sailing & the Guna | TravelWell.World","search_language":"es-PA","local_keywords":["San Blas Guna Yala","islas San Blas Panamá","velero San Blas Cartagena","cómo llegar a San Blas desde Ciudad de Panamá","cabañas San Blas Guna Yala","molas guna","Cayos Holandeses"],"long_tail_en":["how to get to San Blas islands from Panama City","San Blas to Cartagena sailing trip","best San Blas islands for snorkeling","Isla Perro shipwreck snorkel","private catamaran charter San Blas","is San Blas Panama safe"],"hreflang":["en","es-PA"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"type":"private crewed catamaran","name":"ZENITH / CruiseSanBlas / Charter in San Blas","note":"the luxury vehicle in Guna Yala — no branded ultra property exists","earning":"private-charter / CLIA lane"},{"type":"Panama City bookend hotel","name":"American Trade Hotel (Casco Viejo, Small Luxury Hotels of the World)","note":"consortia/Virtuoso-adjacent luxury anchor for the city night","earning":"Fora / consortia hotel commission"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"San Blas / Guna Yala, Panama, Panama"},"geo":{"lat":9.57,"lng":-78.95}}'::jsonb, 97),
  ('san-cristobal-de-las-casas-mexico', '10S', 'San Cristóbal de las Casas, Mexico', 'Mexico', 'San Cristóbal de las Casas', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Chiapas (San Cristóbal & Palenque)', '{"culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_named_area_language":"US govt employees may travel to Tapachula (city limits, S/W of Hwy 200); may NOT travel to municipality of Ocozocoautla; may NOT travel to Southeastern Chiapas polygon (Guatemala border Pacific->Netzahualcoyotl->Ocosingo->El Ocote->San Francisco Pujiltic->Mapastepec, E/N of Hwy 200). San Cristobal / Tuxtla / Chiapa de Corzo fall OUTSIDE named boundaries.","gate_decision":"BOOK WITH WARNING","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","consent_flow":{"disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live advisory + traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"content_only":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Tuxtla Gutierrez TGZ (Angel Albino Corzo Intl) ~77km / ~1h05-1h30 to San Cristobal via Hwy 190/190D; corridor outside restricted zone","road_safety_flag":"Hwy 199 San Cristobal<->Palenque via Ocosingo: reported armed robbery (mostly night) + CNTE blockades — daytime-only, guided/private transfer","altitude":"~2200m, mild","water":"bottled/purified only","dengue":"lowland concern (Palenque/jungle/canyon), not highland city","founder_attorney_flag":"consent-flow wording pending compliance-attorney sign-off; re-verify advisory before each fire and before live checkout","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":["Nov-Apr dry season","Dia de Muertos (Oct 31-Nov 2)","Semana Santa (2026: Mar 29-Apr 5)"],"inflection":"6-10 weeks pre-peak; boutique tier sells 8-12 weeks out","fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (dry-season fire ~mid-Sep; Dia de Muertos fire ~early-mid Oct; Semana Santa 2026 fire ~early-mid Mar) — proceeds with mandatory L3 disclosure","off_season":"May-Oct green/rainy value window; culture fully accessible year-round; highland climate never hot"},"jewels":[{"name":"Andadores + Templo de Santo Domingo + Museo del Ámbar","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://randomtrip.net/san-cristobal-de-las-casas-travel-guide-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"city walking tour + hotel + shopping affiliate (live behind BWW)"},{"name":"San Juan Chamula syncretic church","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://bucketlistbri.com/san-juan-chamula-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"guided community day tour ~US$65pp (live); community fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Zinacantán weaving co-op","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://bucketlistbri.com/zinacantan-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"Chamula+Zinacantán combo tour + co-op purchase (live)"},{"name":"Kakaw Museo del Cacao + café/chocolate culture","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://randomtrip.net/san-cristobal-de-las-casas-travel-guide-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"food/cultural experience affiliate + retail"},{"name":"Chiapa de Corzo (UNESCO / Pueblo Mágico)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Chiapas-attractions/Sumidero-Canyon-National-Park/d5506-a14134","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"paired with Sumidero day tour (DMC/affiliate, live)"},{"name":"Sumidero Canyon boat cruise","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.voyagemexique.info/en/sumidero-canyon/","hook":"2-hour open-boat cruise — life jackets, seated ride, weather-dependent; low risk with licensed operators from Chiapa de Corzo. Guided","si":"expedition","blurb":"2-hour open-boat cruise — life jackets, seated ride, weather-dependent; low risk with licensed operators from Chiapa de Corzo. Guided","commission":"guided boat tour commissionable (live); park/boat federal fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Lagos de Montebello","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.voyagemexique.info/en/sumidero-canyon/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"guided long-day tour DMC (live) — keep to established tourist route near border"},{"name":"El Chiflón waterfalls","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.voyagemexique.info/en/sumidero-canyon/","si":"expedition","commission":"guided day tour DMC/affiliate (live) + entrance non-commissionable"},{"name":"El Arcotete / Rancho Nuevo","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://randomtrip.net/san-cristobal-de-las-casas-travel-guide-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"local guide/transfer affiliate + entrance (live)"},{"name":"Temazcal + boutique-casa spa evenings","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"http://www.casadelalmahotelboutiqueandspa.com/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"romance","when":"year-round","commission":"hotel + spa package direct/DMC (live)"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for — is the road dangerous?","a":"The connective road is the risk, not the city. Highway 199 between San Cristóbal and Palenque via Ocosingo has reported armed robberies (predominantly at night) plus periodic CNTE union blockades that usually cause only short delays. The rule is daytime-only overland travel with a vetted guide or private transfer, never a night self-drive; the city center itself is pedestrian-comfortable by day.","source":"aboutsancristobal.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What are San Juan Chamula and Zinacantán, and how do I visit respectfully?","a":"They are living Tzotzil Maya villages, 10 km out, and a guide is effectively mandatory. Chamula''s church is a pine-needle-floored space of Maya-Catholic fusion with ritual healings day and night and a strict no-photography rule inside; Zinacantán (99% Indigenous) is a backstrap-loom weaving town with a women''s co-op. Pay the community fees and follow a guide who knows the etiquette.","source":"wandersmiles.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What is there to do in the city itself?","a":"Walk the pedestrian andadores — Real de Guadalupe and the Andador Eclesiástico — between two hillside churches. The Templo de Santo Domingo has Chiapas''s most elaborate carved pink facade with a Tzotzil/Tzeltal textile market at its churchyard, and the Museo del Ámbar (in the ex-convent of La Merced) shows amber with 25-million-year-old inclusions, alongside a strong Chiapas-coffee and cacao café culture.","source":"randomtrip.net, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What is Sumidero Canyon, and is it worth it?","a":"Yes — it''s the region''s signature nature outing. A 2-hour open-boat cruise from the UNESCO colonial town of Chiapa de Corzo runs ~32 km beneath canyon walls up to ~1,000 m, past waterfalls and wildlife. It''s a low-risk daytime trip with licensed operators — life vests on, weather-dependent.","source":"voyagemexique.info, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is San Cristóbal a good base for a quiet, cultured couple''s trip?","a":"Yes — it''s cultured romance, not resort romance. At 2,200 m the highland evenings ask for a sweater; boutique colonial casas like Hotel Bö and Casa del Alma offer temazcal spa culture and courtyard dinners along cobblestone andadores. Come in the dry season (Nov–April), with crisp 18–24°C days, blue skies and minimal rain.","source":"climatestotravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Does the altitude affect visitors?","a":"Only mildly. At ~2,200 m some travelers feel light shortness of breath or a disturbed first night''s sleep, but it is not a serious altitude risk — hydrate and ease into exertion on day one. Drink bottled water only; dengue is a lowland concern (Palenque, the canyon), not the cool highland city.","source":"climatestotravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Cristóbal de las Casas, Mexico: Highland Chiapas, Maya Culture & Sumidero Canyon | TravelWell","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en San Cristóbal de las Casas","Cañón del Sumidero","San Juan Chamula","Zinacantán tejido","Lagos de Montebello","El Chiflón cascadas","hoteles boutique San Cristóbal","mejor época para viajar a Chiapas","es seguro San Cristóbal de las Casas"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"San Cristóbal de las Casas"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Hotel Bö","tier":"design-luxury boutique (not global 5-star)","earning":"Fora/Virtuoso consortia commission where participating; else bedbank/OTA","mor":true},{"name":"Casa del Alma Hotel Boutique & Spa","tier":"upper-mid spa boutique","earning":"consortia/agency commission or bedbank","mor":true},{"name":"Hotel Na Bolom","tier":"mid heritage/character","earning":"direct/OTA thin commission, high narrative value","mor":true},{"name":"Private-DMC program (Plan South America / bespoke)","tier":"ultra ground handle incl. private charter SC<->Palenque ~40min","earning":"MoR on itinerary not bed","mor":true}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"San Cristóbal de las Casas, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":16.737,"lng":-92.6376}}'::jsonb, 98),
  ('san-ignacio-belize', '10S', 'San Ignacio / Cayo, Belize', 'Belize', 'Belize''s inland adventure capital', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Belize', '{"expedition","culture","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Base for Actun Tunichil Muknal (ATM) — a guided-only Maya sacrificial cave holding the calcified ''Crystal Maiden'' skeleton near San Ignacio, Cayo District.","Xunantunich''s El Castillo (~40 m) is Belize''s 2nd-tallest structure; reached by a hand-cranked Mopan River ferry ~20 min from town.","Caracol''s Caana pyramid (141 ft / 43 m) is Belize''s tallest structure; access via military-escorted convoy from Douglas D''Silva Forest Station (~9 am) due to Guatemala-border proximity.","Blancaneaux Lodge, a ~20-room hideaway in the Mountain Pine Ridge, was bought by Francis Ford Coppola in the early 1980s and opened to guests in 1993.","BZE (Belize International) to San Ignacio is a ~2-hour drive west on the Western/George Price Highway; the Cayo caves are accessible year-round."],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (verify)","hospital":"San Ignacio Community Hospital (local); trauma to Belize City (~2 hrs) or air-medical evac to Belize City / Guatemala City (verify)","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for the country (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance), pulled live, plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"state_dept_carveout":"only Southside Belize City restricted; Cayo open","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":"BZE -> San Ignacio ~2 hr drive, Western/George Price Highway; regional airstrip Maya Flats (verify)","guatemala_border_note":"Caracol requires military-escorted convoy; Xunantunich near border — disclose, verify current","malaria":"CDC: malaria a risk in SOME parts of Belize; treat mainland jungle as potential risk, advise travel-medicine consult","dengue":"present; mosquito-bite avoidance essential","vaccines":"Hepatitis A (all 1+), typhoid (rural/smaller-city) recommended","water":"bottled/treated only; avoid swimming in fresh unchlorinated water (leptospirosis) — ATM/cave-tubing are unavoidable-immersion guided activities","founder_policy_note":"book_enabled rides on the BOOK WITH WARNING bin (Four-Bin v3): full verbatim live US State Dept advisory disclosed + acknowledged at booking; only Southside Belize City is the named danger"},"timing":{"curve_shape":"dry-season inland spike (cave/road passability), not beach-weather driven","peak":"Dec-Apr dry season; Dec-Jan crowd/price peak; Feb-Mar balanced sweet spot","green_season":"Jun-Nov wet; caves accessible year-round and especially evocative Jun-Oct at high water; rates drop","hurricane_overlay":"Jun-Nov; Sep-Oct highest risk; direct Belize landfalls historically infrequent","fire_date":"~2026-11-20 (primary, dry-season ramp); secondary pulse ~late May (green-season value)","sharpen_note":"season boundaries drift; confirm cave-tour operating status + road passability on live operator advisories before each fire date"},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Actun Tunichil Muknal (ATM) — Crystal Maiden","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Actun_Tunichil_Muknal","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"licensed DMC / lodge tour desk (~$164 pp)"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Cave-tubing (Caves Branch / Cayo)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.pacztours.net/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"DMC day-tour + lodge bundle"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Barton Creek Cave (canoe-through)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.pacztours.net/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Paddled by canoe through a river cave with Maya archaeological remains — guided only","si":"expedition","blurb":"Paddled by canoe through a river cave with Maya archaeological remains — guided only","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"licensed DMC tour"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Mountain Pine Ridge + Rio On Pools + Rio Frio Cave + Big Rock Falls","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/jungle-lodges-belize/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"DMC 4x4 day tour / lodge-based"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Horseback riding (Macal/Mopan valleys)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://chaacreek.com/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"lodge activity / DMC"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Xunantunich + El Castillo + hand-cranked ferry","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.nayawalk.com/belize/xunantunich/","hook":"The Classic Maya city sits near the Belize–Guatemala border","si":"culture","blurb":"The Classic Maya city sits near the Belize–Guatemala border","commission":"DMC half-day / lodge tour"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Caracol — Caana (Belize''s tallest structure)","tier":"premier","source":"https://trans-americas.com/caracol-archaeological-site-belize/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Reached only by military-escorted convoy from the Douglas D''Silva Forest Station because of Guatemala-border proximity","si":"culture","blurb":"Reached only by military-escorted convoy from the Douglas D''Silva Forest Station because of Guatemala-border proximity","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"licensed DMC full-day + convoy logistics"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Cahal Pech (walking distance from town)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.stleonardsbelize.com/belize-tours/xunantunich-cahal-pech-tour","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"self-guided fee / add-on guided walk"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Tikal day-trip (Guatemala)","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.pacztours.net/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"licensed DMC full-day cross-border"},{"si_tag":"Romance & Nature","name":"Green Iguana Conservation Project","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.sanignaciobelize.com/green-iguana-conservation-project/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Romance & Nature","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"in-town lodge activity / affiliate"},{"si_tag":"Romance & Nature","name":"Belize Botanic Gardens at du Plooy''s","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.sanignaciobelize.com/","si":"Romance & Nature","commission":"lodge stay / day visit / bedbank"},{"si_tag":"Romance & Nature","name":"Chaa Creek Butterfly Farm + Macal River canoe","tier":"comfort","source":"https://chaacreek.com/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Romance & Nature","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"lodge stay + activity"},{"si_tag":"Romance & Nature","name":"Spanish Lookout (Mennonite community)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/belize/western-belize/san-ignacio-cayo/attractions/green-iguana-conservation-project/a/poi-sig/460812/358218","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"Romance & Nature","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC add-on / self-drive"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the ATM cave tour like, and do you need a guide?","a":"It is the apex Cayo adventure and it is guided-only by law — you cannot legally enter Actun Tunichil Muknal without a licensed operator. Expect a ~45-minute jungle trek with multiple river crossings, a swim into the cave mouth, wading a shallow underground river in total darkness, and tight climbs; ~3 hours inside. Cameras have been banned since a 2012 incident cracked a ~1,000-year-old skull.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"How do you visit Caracol and Xunantunich?","a":"Differently. Caracol — whose Caana pyramid (141 ft/43 m) is Belize''s tallest structure — requires a military-escorted convoy from the Douglas D''Silva Forest Station (muster ~9 am, return ~2 pm) because it sits near the porous Guatemala border. Xunantunich is easier: a 20-minute drive and a hand-cranked Mopan River ferry to El Castillo, ~40 m and the country''s second-tallest structure.","source":"trans-americas.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is San Ignacio good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — for jungle romance rather than beach. The luxury lodge belt is world-class: Coppola''s Blancaneaux Lodge (~20 rooms, Mountain Pine Ridge waterfalls), the 500-acre Green Globe reserve at Chaa Creek (founded 1981, with butterfly farm, spa and Macal River canoeing), and Ka''ana''s plunge-pool villas. Plunge-pool casitas, canopy dinners and waterfall spas define the market.","source":"chaacreek.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Cayo?","a":"Water, wildlife and inland health, not urban crime. CDC advises avoiding swimming in fresh, unchlorinated water (leptospirosis), yet ATM and cave-tubing involve unavoidable river immersion, so treat them as guided-only informed-consent activities; high water after heavy rain periodically closes the caves. CDC also states malaria is a risk in some parts of Belize — treat the mainland jungle as potential risk and get a travel-medicine consult; dengue is present.","source":"wwwnc.cdc.gov, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the ATM cave tour dangerous?","a":"It is physically demanding but safe as a licensed, guided activity — there is no legal or safe self-tour option. The tour requires \"good to very good\" fitness for river fordings, swimming into the cave, and tight passages and climbs in the upper chambers, with a minimum height of ~40 inches. Cave-tubing and Barton Creek Cave are likewise licensed-guide-required, with rising-water hazard after rain.","source":"chaacreek.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Ignacio & Cayo, Belize: ATM Cave, Xunantunich, Caracol & Jungle Lodges | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Belize''s inland adventure capital — swim into the Crystal Maiden''s cave, climb Caracol and Xunantunich, sleep in Coppola''s jungle hideaway. Guided-only cave tours, luxury eco-lodges, how to travel Cayo well.","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["San Ignacio Belize","Cayo District adventure","ATM cave tour","Actun Tunichil Muknal Crystal Maiden","Xunantunich hand-cranked ferry","Caracol military convoy","Blancaneaux Lodge Belize","cave tubing Belize","best jungle lodges San Ignacio","is Cayo Belize safe 2026"],"hreflang":["en","es-419 (optional)"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","Culture & Heritage (future)","romance"],"ultra":[{"name":"Blancaneaux Lodge","why":"~20-room Coppola hideaway, Mountain Pine Ridge, waterfall pools","earning_path":"Family Coppola Hideaways direct + consortia/Fora lane","mor":"direct-to-lodge","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Ka''ana Resort","why":"18 suites/villas, private plunge pools, boutique 17-acre estate","earning_path":"consortia/Fora + direct","mor":"direct","tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"The Lodge at Chaa Creek","why":"500-acre Green Globe reserve, Macal River, spa, villas","earning_path":"direct + advisor consortia","mor":"direct/AOR","tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"Gaïa Riverlodge","why":"Small Luxury Hotels of the World; 16 cabanas atop Five Sisters Falls, hydropowered","earning_path":"SLH channel + consortia","mor":"SLH/direct","tier":"premier"},{"name":"Table Rock Jungle Lodge","why":"intimate boutique Macal-riverfront cabañas","earning_path":"direct commission","mor":"direct","tier":"comfort"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"San Ignacio / Cayo, Belize, Belize"},"geo":{"lat":17.1598,"lng":-89.0714}}'::jsonb, 99),
