ia","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"commissionable combo day-tour + retail","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is San José worth staying a night, or just an airport?","a":"Worth a night. It''s the front door, not the destination — but the Pre-Columbian Gold Museum (~1,600 pieces, beside the Teatro Nacional), a three-museum pass (~$33), and the Barrio Escalante restaurant row give a genuine half-to-full day of culture-and-coffee substance.","source":"lonelyplanet.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Can you day-trip Poás and Irazú volcanoes from San José?","a":"Yes — both are same-day from the capital. Irazú tops 3,432 m with both oceans visible on a clear morning; Poás runs a dynamic-access, online-only timed-entry model via SINAC, so go guided to absorb the timed-entry and closure logistics.","source":"machupicchu.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where is SJO airport and how busy does it get?","a":"Juan Santamaría (SJO) is Costa Rica''s primary international gateway, 20 km northwest of downtown in Alajuela. It just set a record, handling 3,215,208 international passengers between Nov 2025 and Apr 5 2026 — up 7.9% year-over-year — so book gateway beds and transfers ahead of the dry-season wave.","source":"ticotimes.net, 2026-07-06","si_tag":null},{"q":"If something goes wrong in Costa Rica, is medical care nearby?","a":"Reassuringly, yes — San José IS the national medical and evacuation hub. Hospital Clínica Bíblica (founded 1929, JCI-accredited, 24/7, with an on-site heliport for evac) and the US-affiliated Hospital CIMA are both in the metro, so serious care and the evac hub are right here.","source":"internationalinsurance.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San José & Costa Rica''s Central Valley: Volcanoes, Coffee Tours & the Gateway to Pura Vida | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Poás & Irazú volcanoes, Doka & Café Britt coffee estates, the Gold & Jade museums, and Pacua